Quickstart

Generate an API key and make your first call

Generate an API Key

[card] Get your Fathom API Key
Head to the API Access section of your User Settings and generate an API key.
[!TIP]
API keys are scoped to the user who creates them. Your key can only access meetings you've recorded or that have been shared with you or your Team.   Admins can access all users' shared meetings by configuring View permissions. API keys never grant access to other users' private meetings.

List recent meetings

List the 10 most recent meetings recorded by you or shared to your team.
curl api.fathom.ai/external/v1/meetings \
     -H "X-Api-Key: YOUR_API_KEY"
import requests
# List meetings (GET /meetings)
response = requests.get(
  "api.fathom.ai/external/v1/meetings",
  headers={
    "X-Api-Key": "YOUR_API_KEY"
  },
)
print(response.json())
// List meetings (GET /meetings)
const response = await fetch("api.fathom.ai/external/v1/meetings", {
  method: "GET",
  headers: {
    "X-Api-Key": "YOUR_API_KEY"
  },
});
const body = await response.json();
console.log(body);
[!NOTE]
Replace YOUR_API_KEY with the API key you generated above.
